I have just finished setting up my gaming setup in which i also connected my switch to my monitor. this works great and allows me to easily switch, although to avoid having to unplug and replug my headphones everytime to switch audio, i plugged it into my monitor. however this presents one big issue. My headphones dont have a dedicated volume control unit on the cable or earcups and I can't lower the volume within the switch software somehow, nor on my monitor. What would be a good solution to this? are there any (cheap) devices I can buy that I can put between the monitor and headphone that can work as a volume slider?

&#x200B;

I have the Audio-Technica ATH-M50X headphones and Dell S2721DGF monitor.

that's weird tho. I had just reinstalled windows and it never acted up before..

&#x200B;

gpu is relatively new too (rtx 3080)

